; plugin.def — export exactly the entry point Photoshop/Affinity look up via
; the PiPL's '8664' (Win64 code) property. Using a .def guarantees the exact
; undecorated export name regardless of compiler/calling-convention quirks.
;
; No LIBRARY statement, on purpose. With one, the linker takes that name as the
; image's internal name and writes it into the .exp, so `LIBRARY spektrafilm`
; produced /OUT:spektrafilm.dll against an output file called spektrafilm.8bf and
; MSVC reported LNK4070 on every build. Leaving it out makes the linker use the
; output file name, so the two cannot disagree. (Naming it `spektrafilm.8bf`
; would work for link.exe but GNU ld rejects the dot in a LIBRARY name, and this
; file is shared with the mingw validation build.)
EXPORTS
    PluginMain
